# promise: #788
# The sidebar's "+ New Tab" row under the pointer: an ordinary hovered row, a shade darker with its muted ink,
# as in Arc 1.174.1. Cra painted it white with the primary ink, the selected tab's look, which belongs to the row
# only while ⌘T's bar is open (#47). Hovered as if the pointer were on it, then with the bar open.
budget rss=600 stalls50=10
cra://debug?windowSize=1280x800
cra://import?source=arc&archive=0&settings=0
wait 2
cra://action/space2
wait 2
cra://debug?newTabRow=rest
expect-log new tab row rest: fill=clear ink=secondary lifted=0 hovered=0
cra://debug?hover=NewTabRowView
wait 1
cra://debug?newTabRow=hovered
expect-log new tab row hovered: fill=hover ink=secondary lifted=0 hovered=1
cra://commandbar
wait 1
cra://debug?newTabRow=bar
expect-log new tab row bar: fill=selected ink=primary lifted=1
cra://dismiss
